course: dictionary
lesson: 12239
title: Consistently: the same every time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When something happens in the same way every time, again and again, we say it happens consistently. Look at the clue words around it. «Mia is consistently kind to her little brother.» The words "kind to her little brother" tell you what she is like, and "consistently" tells you she is kind every time, not just now and then.
explain: The word comes from "consistent", which means "always the same" or "not changing". Add "-ly" and it becomes an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. «The bus is consistently late on Mondays.» It is late on every Monday, so consistently means it happens again and again without changing.
explain: A second meaning is about agreeing with itself. A story is consistent when its details match and nothing contradicts another part. If a character is brave in chapter one and a coward in chapter two with no reason, the story is not consistent. To check the meaning, swap in "in the same way every time" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Consistently means in the same way every time, again and again, without changing.
fact: «Consistently» is an adverb. Its adjective is «consistent», and its noun is «consistency».
fact: Results that are consistently the same are reliable, so scientists value them.
fact: A story or set of facts is consistent when its parts agree and do not contradict each other.
fact: Phrases you may see include «consistently good», «consistently late» and «consistently high».
exercise: «Mia is consistently kind to her little brother.» What does consistently mean? | Once, by accident | Loudly and angrily | Only sometimes | *Every time, in the same way
exercise: Ben's teacher writes, «Ben works consistently hard.» What does consistently tell us? | Ben stops working early | Ben works hard in the morning only | Ben works hard only once | *Ben works hard every time
exercise: «The bus is consistently late on Mondays.» Find and copy the one word that tells us how the bus is late every time. | late | *consistently | Mondays | bus
test: «The sun rises consistently in the east.» What does consistently suggest? | Very quickly | Once in a while | *Every day, without changing | Only in the summer
test: Which word is the adjective that goes with consistently? | consist | *consistent | consistency | consistently
exam: «Sara's spelling is consistently good, so her teacher says she can be trusted.» Which phrase best means the same as consistently here? | just this once | in a loud voice | after a long wait | *in the same good way every time
